Article 30
Every Child has the right to receive Special Protection.
(1) Children who require Special Protection (2) as referred to in paragraph (1) include: a. Children in emergency situations;
b. Children in conflict with the law;
c. Children from minority and isolated groups;
d. Children who are exploited economically and/or sexually;
e. Children who are victims of narcotics, alcohol, psychotropic substances, and other addictive substances abuse; f. Children who are victims of pornography;
g. Children with human immunodeficiency virus (HIV)/
h. acquired immuno deficiency syndrome (AIDS); i. Children victims of kidnapping, sale, and/or trafficking;
j. Children victims of physical and/or psychological violence;
k. Children victims of sexual crimes;
l. Children victims of terrorism networks;
m. Children with Disabilities;
n. Children victims of abuse and neglect;
o. Children with deviant social behavior; and
p. Children who are victims of stigmatization from labeling related to their parents' condition.
(3) The forms of Special Protection for Children as referred to in paragraph (2) shall be further regulated by Regent Regulation.
